## 7. Self-critique pass (adversarial review)

The diff was put through a 4-dimension adversarial review
(sla-logic / sql-queries / worker-schema / react-page), every finding
independently re-verified against the code with a concrete failing input. The
sql/worker/react dimensions returned **no confirmed bugs**. The sla-logic
dimension found **4 confirmed, all fixed** — all the same root cause: the first
implementation followed the brief's literal `end = lastActivityMs ?? createdMs`
for Solution Proposed and reused that single `end` for *three* jobs.

**Fixed (all sla-logic, high-confidence):**

1. **(blocker) Missed initial response masked.** A Resolved case Infor never
   answered, with an early *customer* post, got `end = created + 1h`, so the
   no-response initial check (`end − created > initialMs`) evaluated `1h > 2h` =
   false and silently passed SLA. **Fix:** the initial-response check now anchors
   to the **snapshot** (`baseEnd`), not the clock-stop. Restores the `'initial'`
   breach.
2. **(major) Late customer reply fabricated a cadence breach.** With `end =`
   last activity (any author), a customer reply long after the last Infor update
   made `end − ts[last] > cadence` → a false `'cadence'` breach on a case Infor
   correctly stopped updating. **Fix:** the cadence trailing gap now anchors to the
   last **Infor** update (`ts[last]`) → gap zero.
3. **(major) CSV-path source divergence.** `last_activity_ms` read `work_notes`
   while the cadence timeline read `additional_comments` — distinct fields on the
   CSV import path (only identical on XLSX), producing negative/incoherent trailing
   gaps that hid or fabricated breaches. **Fix:** `parseLastActivity` scans the
   journal **union** (`jiraJournals(r)`), and cadence no longer depends on it at all.
4. **(major) Backdated journal masked breaches / pre-dated auto-close.** A journal
   header before `created` drove `end < created`, making the end-anchored checks go
   negative (no breach), and started the 90-day countdown before the case existed.
   **Fix:** `computeSlaSop` no longer uses last activity for either SLA anchor; the
   auto-close anchor is clamped `Math.max(lastActivity, created)` in `enrich.js` and
   `greatest(…)` in the SQL.

**Consolidated fix:** `computeSlaSop` no longer takes the auto-close anchor at all —
the cadence anchor is `ts[last]` (Infor-only) and the initial anchor is the
snapshot/close. The auto-close countdown is a *separate* concern; it was initially
the all-author last activity, then **revised to the resolution-notes-saved time**
(`resolved_at_ms`) after the user's domain caveat (§3 / §3a). Each finding gained a
regression fixture (F1–F4) in the test suite. The fix is a single change in
`computeSlaSop` (one source of truth), so `enrichRow`/`enrichForSql` parity is
preserved automatically.

> **Deviation from the brief (documented):** the brief specified
> `end = isSolutionProposed ? (lastActivityMs ?? createdMs) : …`. That literal
> formula is the source of all four bugs; the corrected design preserves the
> brief's *intent* (no trailing-idle breach; pre-resolution gaps + initial misses
> still judged) while being correct on customer-late, CSV-divergent, never-answered,
> and backdated rows.

