## 8. Test coverage

`src/lib/enrich.sla-solution-proposed.test.js` — 18 tests, `node --test`, no new deps:

- **Direct `computeSlaSop`** — clock-stop (identical inputs breach when OPEN, pass when Solution Proposed), pre-resolution inter-update gap still breaches, never-answered → `'initial'`, late non-Infor anchor can't move the trailing gap.
- **`parseResolutionTime`** — null/no-marker → null, latest marker wins, reminders ignored; plus `parseInforUpdates`/`parseInteractions` exclude System auto-reminder authors.
- **Pipeline (1)–(7) + (F1)–(F4)** — healthy-idle (no cadence breach, `dueSop` null), initial-miss, pre-resolution gap, open-case regression, **parity** (`enrichRow` ≡ `enrichForSql` on `sla_eligible`/`sla_breached`/`sla_due_sop`/`resolved_at_ms` + the BigInt/Date type split), auto-close = resolution + 90d & countdown sign, null-journal fallback + initial miss, and the caveat regressions: a late customer reply / system reminder does not move the anchor (F2), a Work-notes reminder doesn't either (F3), a backdated marker clamps to created (F4), and System reminders are excluded from `parseInforUpdates`/`parseInteractions`.
- **(F1)–(F4)** — the four adversarial-review regressions above, each with a parity assertion where the two journal fields diverge.

The `getSolutionProposedAutoClose` SQL is browser-runtime (DuckDB-WASM), outside
`node --test`; it was validated with a throwaway Node-blocking DuckDB harness
(analyst scope, `__all__`, empty, OPEN/CLOSED exclusion, null fallback, backdated
clamp, soonest-first/NULLS-LAST ordering) and is exercised live in the manual QA.

